stage: 4
finding: Direct NormalTrack no longer enforces that excluded is a list. The old graph runtime rejected non-arrays at the list input boundary; the new expression forwards excluded to ties/repeatDistances, which spreads it for validation and later calls .some. An empty string (or a Set when no candidate reaches the filter) can therefore pass validation and return a construction; for the empty string, every candidate sees a falsy .some result only if no candidate reaches it, e.g. a short path with startOffset beyond its length. The named tests pass but do not cover malformed excluded containers on empty repeats, so the previous domain/atomic refusal is not preserved.
